-- ============================================================================
-- QI EXPERT DEEP SEED: Quantitative Interpretation, advanced tier.
--
-- Six modules, 26 lessons, 132 questions (15 per module bank plus a 42
-- question final exam). The structure row is GENERATED from the tier's
-- manifest.json rather than hand typed, and the question rows from the
-- committed bank JSONs under tools/course-banks/qi/advanced.
--
-- What this tier owns: INVERSION, PROPERTIES AND THE DECISION. The
-- convolutional model and its adjoint, the low-frequency model and the wavelet
-- scale; model-based, sparse-spike and coloured inversion, blind wells,
-- quantiles across realisations; Fatti's simultaneous inversion; property
-- transforms with their intervals, left-out wells, Bayesian facies and the
-- confusion matrix; closure, anomaly conformance, evidence and the assessment;
-- the report and what QI never sets.
--
-- AN APP COURSE. The Suite app is QI Studio; the practicals also run in the
-- course's own explorer panels. The tier's capstone grades six values on a
-- held-out synthetic case, each a return value of a vendored engine. No BEGIN
-- or COMMIT: apply_qi.sh wraps this file in one transaction.
-- ============================================================================

values ('qi', 'advanced', '{"modules":[{"key":"m01-the-forward-model","title":"The Forward Model","lesson_keys":["l01-what-the-expert-tier-adds","l02-the-convolutional-model-and-its-adjoint","l03-the-low-frequency-model","l04-the-wavelet-scale"]},{"key":"m02-post-stack-inversion","title":"Post-Stack Inversion","lesson_keys":["l01-model-based-least-squares","l02-blocky-and-sparse-spike","l03-coloured-inversion","l04-blind-wells","l05-sensitivity-across-realisations"]},{"key":"m03-simultaneous-inversion","title":"Simultaneous Inversion","lesson_keys":["l01-fattis-three-parameters","l02-angle-dependent-wavelets","l03-why-density-needs-the-far-angles","l04-blind-wells-per-parameter"]},{"key":"m04-properties-from-impedance","title":"Properties from Impedance","lesson_keys":["l01-a-linear-transform-and-its-interval","l02-left-out-wells-and-the-widened-band","l03-bayesian-facies-on-impedance","l04-two-attributes","l05-the-confusion-matrix-and-a-fluid-hypothesis"]},{"key":"m05-prospects","title":"Prospects","lesson_keys":["l01-crest-spill-and-closure","l02-anomaly-conformance-and-the-implied-contact","l03-independent-evidence-and-competing-explanations","l04-the-qi-assessment"]},{"key":"m06-the-report-and-the-limits","title":"The Report and the Limits","lesson_keys":["l01-the-qi-report-and-the-handover-files","l02-what-qi-never-sets","l03-what-the-engines-do-not-compute","l04-the-capstone-brief"]}]}'::jsonb, 1)
on conflict (app_slug, tier) do update
  set structure = excluded.structure,
      content_version = excluded.content_version,
      active = true,
      updated_at = now();

delete from public.academy_quiz_questions
 where app_slug = 'qi' and tier = 'advanced';

